    "status": "mapped",
    "locations": [
      {
        "chapter": 42,
        "section": "High-Yield Hits",
        "items": [
          15,
          16,
          17,
          20
        ]
      }
    ],
    "note": "Teaches Ch. 42 Hit 15 (donor Hb minimum — corrected), Hit 16 (eligibility checklist), Hit 17 (donation interval) and Hit 20 (autologous Hb). Checked against 21 CFR 630.10 and 630.15 (eCFR, read 2026-10-08). Hit 15 corrected: 12.5 g/dL / 38% applies to female allogeneic donors; male allogeneic donors need 13.0 g/dL / 39% (register flag rv-donor-hb). Not taught: age (set by state law, not 630.10), 10-minute collection limit, vasovagal management, directed donors (not verified). These are US rules; the Philippine (MTLE) criteria were not checked."
  },
  "prerequisites": [],
  "objectives": [
    "State the US FDA donor vital-sign and weight minimums.",
    "Apply sex-specific and autologous hemoglobin/hematocrit minimums.",
    "State acceptable hemoglobin sample types.",
    "Apply whole-blood and double red-cell donation intervals."
  ],
