    {
      "id": "normal",
      "kind": "normal",
      "title": "Normal: two people to protect",
      "start": 20,
      "end": 60,
      "altText": "A scale balancing two cards: “Donor safety” and “Product potency (and recipient safety)”. Checklist tokens appear under donor safety: temperature, blood pressure, pulse, hemoglobin/hematocrit, weight, skin at the phlebotomy site. A note: these are US FDA minimums (21 CFR 630.10); collectors can be stricter and other countries differ.",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": "n1",
          "start": 20,
          "end": 30,
          "text": "Every donor rule protects two people: the donor, who must stay well after giving blood, and the recipient, who needs a safe, effective product."
        },
        {
          "id": "n2",
          "start": 30,
          "end": 40,
          "text": "So on the day of donation, before collection, the donor is checked: temperature, blood pressure, pulse, hemoglobin or hematocrit, weight, and the skin at the needle site."
        },
        {
          "id": "n3",
          "start": 40,
          "end": 50,
          "text": "The hemoglobin check guards both: it protects the donor from becoming anemic and ensures the unit carries enough red cells."
        },
        {
          "id": "n4",
          "start": 50,
          "end": 60,
          "text": "These are the US FDA minimums. Blood collectors may be stricter, and other countries set their own rules."
        }
      ],
